cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Nexus SymBiote in research or in a security program, cite this
  repository. The project is alpha software: cite the exact version or commit
  you used.
title: Nexus SymBiote
type: software
authors:
  - name: AISecNomad
    website: https://github.com/aisecnomad
repository-code: https://github.com/aisecnomad/Nexus-symbiote
url: https://github.com/aisecnomad/Nexus-symbiote
abstract: >-
  Nexus SymBiote builds an Agent Bill of Materials (AgentBOM, AIBOM) for AI
  agent projects from static evidence: MCP configuration, model artifacts,
  prompts and skills, retrieval configuration, package manifests, A2A cards,
  IDE agent configuration, and imported Nexus-ShadowScan reports. It exports
  native JSON, CycloneDX 1.7, SPDX 3.0.1, SARIF, and VEX, validates
  completeness and integrity, scores risk under a policy, and compares
  snapshots. A successful scan is an inventory result, not a safety
  certificate.
keywords:
  - agentbom
  - aibom
  - sbom
  - ai-security
  - supply-chain
  - agentic-ai
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - a2a
  - cyclonedx
  - spdx
  - sarif
  - vex
